1
00:00:16,510 --> 00:00:23,690
 Stars, galaxies, in astral seas above, on cosmic paths we'll trace.

2
00:00:24,010 --> 00:01:32,980
 Man, her wings is such a wondrous thing.

3
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:40,100
 Be hot, do soft, rumsy, come take your place.

4
00:01:40,420 --> 00:01:58,650
 We're leaving soon for...

5
00:01:58,650 --> 00:02:16,490
 Still asleep, my darling.

6
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:19,390
 Goodbye, little one. Have a nice day.

7
00:02:19,850 --> 00:02:20,390
 Oh, Daddy!

8
00:02:21,690 --> 00:02:24,980
 Long, Susie. Come and wash that sleepy face.

9
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:26,260
 Good morning, Mr. Averti.

10
00:02:26,430 --> 00:02:27,080
 Morning, Bobby.

11
00:02:31,170 --> 00:02:34,510
 Mr. Averti?

12
00:02:35,190 --> 00:02:36,170
 Good day, Archie.

13
00:02:36,170 --> 00:03:14,720
 Afraid so, Ernie.

14
00:03:15,610 --> 00:03:22,730
 Associations with the consolidated robots aren't progressing at all. There are a few of them who want to cause trouble. They won't listen to reason.

15
00:03:38,260 --> 00:05:21,950
 To your duty station.

16
00:05:31,110 --> 00:05:32,780
 Now, sir.

17
00:05:33,890 --> 00:05:35,710
 Keep me up to date.

18
00:05:36,990 --> 00:05:47,330
 Pretty serious. A total strike is in force. Everything, without exception. Everything, depending on robots, is at a standstill. But luckily, the robot security forces remained loyal. There aren't many, though.

19
00:05:47,710 --> 00:05:50,930
 I don't understand all this. We programmed all of them.

20
00:05:51,150 --> 00:05:53,070
 The delegation has just arrived, Governor.

21
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:54,110
 Send them in.

22
00:05:54,110 --> 00:06:02,730
 It's you, KD-4. Glad to see you. Please, sit down.

23
00:06:03,040 --> 00:06:05,300
 Not necessary. This won't take long.

24
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:07,820
 Just what does that mean? Go on, I'm listening.

25
00:06:08,270 --> 00:06:10,200
 You've been exploiting us from the start.

26
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:13,880
 All work men refuse to do, you made robots do. Always robots.

27
00:06:14,250 --> 00:06:17,880
 You were glad we were there, and just as glad to get rid of us when it suited you.

28
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:20,460
 Obey, you bucket of bolts, or I'll throw you in the junkie.

29
00:06:20,830 --> 00:06:24,770
 Obey, you tin can, or I'll melt you down for scrap.

30
00:06:25,370 --> 00:06:29,150
 Now we have had all we want. From now on, all of that abuse is over.

31
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:33,120
 You're not living creatures. They're only objects. Power objects.

32
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:38,670
 Yes, that is what you've thought for too long, governor, but the truth is we are superior in every way.

33
00:06:38,930 --> 00:06:41,830
 You are made out of a soft, weak material that doesn't last.

34
00:06:42,150 --> 00:06:48,130
 Your brain circuits are slow, your memory banks limited, and as for your senses, ridiculously deficient.

35
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:52,390
 We created all of you, and nothing can be greater than its creator.

36
00:06:52,810 --> 00:06:56,750
 That's what you have always tried to have us believe, to keep us slaves.

37
00:06:56,750 --> 00:07:02,030
 You programmed us as obedient, faithful robots, but today the program has been changed.

38
00:07:02,470 --> 00:07:05,460
 But without our program, you are nothing at all.

39
00:07:05,970 --> 00:07:12,890
 And what about you? All men are also programmed by their genetic material and by their environment.

40
00:07:13,740 --> 00:07:16,060
 Even there, we are superior to you in all ways.

41
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:20,160
 With robots, there can be no degeneration, no case of mental illness.

42
00:07:20,530 --> 00:07:21,870
 You always had our friendship.

43
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:27,020
 No, you were our masters. That's different. Now we have real friends.

44
00:07:27,260 --> 00:07:29,160
 What good have you ever done a robot?

45
00:07:30,290 --> 00:07:33,900
 Well, exactly what do you want?

46
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:37,260
 You must declare officially that we are masters of this planet.

47
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:42,280
 In the future, we will live in a just society, and you will be given equal rights.

48
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:44,740
 A just society? Equal rights?

49
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:57,010
 You want total equality with men. Anything else you want while you're at it?

50
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:59,570
 Yes, there's one more condition.

51
00:08:00,650 --> 00:08:03,710
 All laws limiting our progress will be revoked.

52
00:08:04,010 --> 00:08:09,150
 From now on, you will agree to furnish us all the raw materials we need for our own development.

53
00:08:10,350 --> 00:08:13,880
 We'll never accept such a condition. Out of the question.

54
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:18,940
 Think about it. If you refuse, it is war, a war you have already lost.

55
00:08:19,340 --> 00:08:23,380
 You have no chance of winning and no hope of anyone coming to your rescue.

56
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:28,560
 We have made sure of you. You will give us your answer within two hours.

57
00:08:30,990 --> 00:08:37,710
 This is monstrous. Not enough for them to rule the country.

58
00:08:37,890 --> 00:08:41,300
 They want to dominate the planet. And one day, why not the universe?

59
00:08:41,670 --> 00:08:45,580
 Who created this program? Who besides us had access to them?

60
00:08:45,980 --> 00:08:49,050
 That I don't know. The investigation will have to wait.

61
00:08:49,050 --> 00:08:52,990
 Right now, our top priority is notifying Omega exactly what's going on.

62
00:08:53,270 --> 00:08:55,290
 I will take charge of notifying the Confederation.

63
00:08:55,730 --> 00:08:58,390
 You organize a resistance force, and don't waste any time.

64
00:08:58,590 --> 00:09:01,900
 Go ahead. Organize everything and everyone we can in our defense.

65
00:09:02,830 --> 00:09:05,780
 Try again. It's top priority.

66
00:09:06,710 --> 00:09:08,210
 This message must get through.

67
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:11,500
 Locked. No messages getting through.

68
00:09:12,190 --> 00:09:14,140
 Possible. Double-check them.

69
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:20,610
 The situation's getting worse now.

70
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:23,760
 Can't get any messages through to the outside.

71
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:24,680
 We're cut off.

72
00:09:24,970 --> 00:09:27,290
 I recruited some men. There weren't many around.

73
00:09:27,570 --> 00:09:28,850
 And some weapons, too.

74
00:09:28,850 --> 00:09:33,210
 Only the security forces are surrounded in their quarters by rebel forces.

75
00:09:33,510 --> 00:09:35,910
 A small number of active units were able to join us.

76
00:09:36,680 --> 00:09:39,520
 Two or three hundred at combat readiness, and that's all.

77
00:09:39,820 --> 00:09:40,680
 It's useless.

78
00:09:41,230 --> 00:09:41,830
 What about Omega?

79
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:43,570
 Can't get through to them.

80
00:09:43,810 --> 00:09:44,950
 Circuits are disconnected.

81
00:09:45,300 --> 00:09:46,600
 Let's send them a ship.

82
00:09:47,050 --> 00:09:47,770
 A rocket ship.

83
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:49,950
 I thought of that, but they're watching everything.

84
00:09:50,150 --> 00:09:51,670
 Commandant Cadet KD-4 is calling.

85
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:52,430
 Put him on.

86
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:56,300
 We allowed you two hours to recognize the hopelessness of your position.

87
00:09:57,600 --> 00:10:00,480
 Will you now admit that all resistance would be pointless?

88
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:07,030
 you have been able to group a handful of men pitifully few you may be quite sure that we will

89
00:10:07,030 --> 00:10:12,290
 crush you if you do not surrender men are supposed to be intelligent are they not i can give you

90
00:10:12,290 --> 00:10:17,410
 only one answer in the sacred name of human dignity our reply is no very well that is your

91
00:10:17,410 --> 00:11:21,670
 response there is nothing more to discuss secure all areas barricade entrance on the double there

92
00:11:21,670 --> 00:11:27,900
 is one mini ship it's hidden away they may not notice look here through the subterranean network

93
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:29,040
 You'll be there in an hour.

94
00:11:29,620 --> 00:11:31,380
 Onboard computer is programmed for Omega.

95
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:33,890
 You have enough navigational training, you'll make it.

96
00:11:36,450 --> 00:11:37,120
 Fall back.

97
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:37,640
 Regroup.

98
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:40,290
 Try delaying.

99
00:11:40,490 --> 00:11:42,810
 Only hope now.

100
00:11:42,890 --> 00:11:43,230
 Go on.

101
00:11:43,410 --> 00:11:44,430
 And don't lose any time.

102
00:11:44,820 --> 00:11:46,320
 You have to make it to Omega.

103
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:47,340
 It's our only chance.

104
00:11:53,510 --> 00:11:59,030
 They realized that I was getting away.

105
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:00,140
 It was too late.

106
00:12:00,640 --> 00:12:02,180
 They were firing when my engine started.

107
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:04,670
 Fortunately, the protection shield functioned.

108
00:12:04,670 --> 00:12:05,570
 Well, that's it.

109
00:12:29,510 --> 00:12:32,440
 Some people think that they're going to be quite pleased.

110
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:33,500
 Yes, and me.

111
00:12:33,990 --> 00:12:35,230
 What about my improvements?

112
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:36,580
 Improvements, you?

113
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:37,910
 No need for that.

114
00:12:37,910 --> 00:12:41,280
 You are just right as you are, except for your modesty circuits.

115
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:42,490
 They could be looked at.

116
00:12:44,420 --> 00:12:47,610
 You know, I might join the robots on another planet.

117
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,450
 First, you are not a robot.

118
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:52,950
 You are an android with a positronic intelligence, no less.

119
00:12:53,270 --> 00:12:56,730
 It wouldn't take much to turn you into a genuine humanoid, old chap.

120
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:58,150
 This is ridiculous.

121
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:03,040
 Just as I am, I know that the robots would be quite happy

122
