 Now, if we suppose, there could be some tampering with their programming.

135
00:13:54,280 --> 00:13:57,700
 Wait a second. Deprogram and reprogram.

136
00:13:58,320 --> 00:14:03,540
 Sit. Can you tell me, recently, these robots underwent any kind of checkup, any adjusting?

137
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:10,270
 Yes. Within the year, the older model KD-2s were all updated, with new modifications so they conform to KD-4s.

138
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:11,680
 But why are you asking the question?

139
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,560
 Why didn't you tell us?

140
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:19,780
 Well, it was just routine. Nothing unusual. Maintenance robots reprogrammed them.

141
00:14:20,260 --> 00:14:23,750
 Well, there's your answer. Why didn't you figure that out for yourself?

142
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:28,970
 Any enemy had only to modify the program in one of the maintenance robots to carry out the whole thing.

143
00:14:29,550 --> 00:14:37,320
 With a few reprogrammed robots in key positions, the men wouldn't be able to detect the short-circuiting of the old program and its replacement by the new one.

144
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:39,660
 Well, what do we do? Go in and rescue them?

145
00:14:39,940 --> 00:14:41,300
 No, they would destroy us.

146
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:44,820
 They have hostages. We must think about them.

147
00:14:45,080 --> 00:14:51,360
 Gotta trick them. Machines are just machines, after all, and what's better than to send a machine to fight a machine?

148
